<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-002-S15-R3>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-002-S15-R3" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "forbidden_daemon_log_entries strings never match real daemon log output" ;
  triage:description "In scripts/smoke/run_peer_pair.py's new semantic-verification mechanism (added on feature/pAI-s15-windows-peer-smoke, commit 12f4b96e), untrusted_or_allowlist_rejection's shipped forbidden_daemon_log_entries strings (\"peer delivery\"/\"duplicate nudge\") match no real daemon log output, so the check can never fail regardless of a real violation -- an always-passing check. Found by req-qa during QA-2 verification of the BLOCKING-02/04 fix on PR #611." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "repo-wide" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-27T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closureNote "2026-07-27 (quality-mgr): ATMQA002-S15R3-QA-1 fix-verification PASS for PR #662 (0920faea) on fix/legacy-atmqa002-smoke-evidence -> integrate/phase-AI. Independently re-verified against the actual code, not self-report. scripts/smoke/run_peer_pair.py's require_semantic_verification now FAILS the config if forbidden_daemon_log_entries is present at all (\"was removed; use required_daemon_log_events or forbidden_daemon_log_events\", line ~198-201), replacing it with require_log_event_selectors: required_daemon_log_events/forbidden_daemon_log_events are structured selector objects matched field-by-field (action/outcome/message/level/service/target/fields) against real parsed JSONL daemon log events via verify_daemon_log_events/daemon_log_event_matches (lines ~325-390), not substring search. Confirmed the untrusted_or_allowlist_rejection case's REJECTION_EVENT selector ({action:request, outcome:rejected, message:'HTTPS peer request was rejected before or during shared API routing', fields.subsystem:https_transport}) matches a real daemon-emitted tracing::warn! event at crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs:566-575 (log_peer_request_result), and ROUTING_EVENT ({action:peer_delivery, outcome:write_persisted}) matches the real DaemonEvent emitted via SubsystemObservability::event(\"peer_delivery\", event.kind.as_str(), ...) in crates/atm-daemon/src/peer_delivery_observability.rs -- these are genuine daemon-side action/outcome literals, not relabeled unmatchable strings. scripts/smoke/test_run_peer_pair.py and .just/tests/test_peer_pair_smoke.py were updated consistently: new tests assert fail-closed behavior for a missing required event, a forbidden event present, and malformed/non-JSONL log delta lines, plus a passing case using a real encoded structured event. docs/peer-pair-smoke.md documents the new exact-selector contract and the concrete real event shape. All 8 GH Actions legs pass at 0920faea; independently re-ran just lint (22/22 pass) and just test locally (120 passed, 1 pre-existing unrelated failure -- peer_resolution::tests::failed_dns_resolution_preserves_the_underlying_cause -- independently reproduced identically on integrate/phase-AI tip, confirmed pre-existing/environmental, not introduced by this diff). Diff touches only scripts/docs, no RSH-002-relevant production code -- no regression risk to that or any other closed finding. Closing as fixed and superseding all 6 repeatable occurrences (s15-s20) on the shared script/test files, since the fix lands at the shared source these branches all reference through integrate/phase-AI." ;
